WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.336
-My next guest is a talented
actor and comedian

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:06.438
who voices one of the characters
in the hit Netflix movie

00:00:06.438 --> 00:00:09.575
"The Mitchells vs The Machines,"
which is streaming now.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.211
Here is Fred Armisen!

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:13.513
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.880
Oh, my God, Fred!

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.916
-Hi. Hi!

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.317
-Come on!

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:20.253
It is so good to see you, bud.

00:00:20.253 --> 00:00:21.420
-It's great to see you.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.922
-How you doing, man?
-What you are up to?

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.123
What are you doing?

00:00:24.123 --> 00:00:25.725
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:28.061
-I'm hosting "The Tonight Show."

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.629
-Aw, that's so great, buddy.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.264
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.765
-You're my guest.

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:33.967
Hey, it's kind of interesting
that --

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.702
your head has never been bigger.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.536
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:38.872
-I had it enlarged.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:39.973
-Wow.

00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:41.174
-Yeah.

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:44.710
-This is pre --
This is pre-pandemic, or...?

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.013
-During pandemic, so dur-pan.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.814
-Oh.
-I just had -- It's really easy.

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:50.450
It's not that much of a hassle.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.418
You just get some shelling...
-Dur-pan.

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:54.820
-...that goes into the forehead

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:56.989
and some sort of shelling
that goes into the sides --

00:00:56.989 --> 00:00:58.425
-Yeah, the shelling.
-It sort of expands.

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:01.961
Yeah, it sort of -- and it --
it takes a day at the most.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.929
I was just out for a little
while, and --

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.064
-If you want, I can --

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:06.799
Fred, I can be your legs
if you want.

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:09.335
Like, maybe if you want to --
-Yeah, let's do that.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:10.603
Can you --

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:11.737
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:13.573
Let's see.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.875
Let's see.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.644
Ah!

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.279
Boy.

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.315
Sure is great,
just stretching out.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:24.884
And got my pants on
and my shoes here.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.552
My shoes look great!

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.121
Aw, man, these are dancing
shoes.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.022
[ Jaunty music plays ]
♪ I like to dance ♪

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:31.958
♪ I like to dance ♪

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.826
♪ Ba da ba, do do do ♪

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.428
♪ I like to dance ♪

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.996
Ah.

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:39.732
Yah, yah, yah.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:40.599
Ooh.

00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:42.468
Oh, boy.

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.870
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, Fred. It's almost like --

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.037
-Thank you.

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:48.408
-It feels like you just
gave birth to me.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.443
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:52.945
Fred, it's good to see you.

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:55.582
I want to talk to you
about Record Store Day.

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:57.550
'Cause you're the ambassador for
Record Store Day.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.186
That's a big deal.
I think it's awesome.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.888
-It's great.
They do it every year.

00:02:01.888 --> 00:02:04.123
And I love going record shopping

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.125
everywhere I go,
wherever I travel.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.927
I really do stop
into a record store.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.362
I know that you're really
into vinyl

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.264
and you've got, like, a whole
record room and everything.

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.498
-I do, I love --
-Right.

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:14.634
-Yeah. What was your first
record? Do you remember?

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.337
-First records I ever got
were Beatles records.

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:19.872
I lived in Brazil.

00:02:19.872 --> 00:02:23.843
And my dad worked for IBM,
so we were there.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.245
And, like, my mom would get me
Beatles records.

00:02:26.245 --> 00:02:28.714
This is sort of post --
right after they broke up,

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:30.783
so there was, like,
Wings records and Beatles.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.051
-Yeah.
-You remember, it was all

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.585
kind of the same thing?

00:02:33.585 --> 00:02:35.154
And so then, I used to --

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:37.523
So this is one of
the first records I got.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:38.991
-"Beatles Forever."
I didn't even know what --

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:40.393
What is that album?

00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:43.262
-It was like a compilation
that they -- that Apple put out.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:44.864
But this was, like,
on the Brazilian label,

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.299
so I used to think that --

00:02:47.299 --> 00:02:49.569
[ Speaking Portuguese ]
-Wow.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.437
-I used to just think
that they all had

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.439
this Portuguese writing on it.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.840
-You know what
we should mention,

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.843
what dates are Record Store Day,
so everyone knows?

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.712
-That's June 12th and July 17th.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.114
-That's right. They're doing it
twice this year.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.381
Good.
I love that you're doing that.

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:03.649
You're a good man.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.384
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.652
-You don't do --
-Oh, I didn't --

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:08.354
I didn't say what year. 2029.

00:03:08.354 --> 00:03:10.823
-No, no, no, we know.
No, no, no, it's this year.

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:12.425
It's 2021. That's not true.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:15.094
Fred, you do voices
and characters.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.829
You also do impressions,
by the way.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.765
And I heard that you're working
on a new impression.

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:21.701
Can you -- Can you maybe
do it for us tonight?

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.802
-Yes, yeah.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.470
So there's an impression
I want to do of --

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.908
These are Instagram ads
that I keep getting. Right?

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.677
So I got to put this back
like this,

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.812
a little bit, if you don't mind.

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.847
I keep -- I don't know
if you get these.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:39.418
But it's like --
if I could get the band

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:42.087
to do, like,
a little Chillwave music,

00:03:42.087 --> 00:03:43.589
'cause they love
demonstrating things.

00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:44.924
[ Band plays soft music ]
-Uh-huh.

00:03:44.924 --> 00:03:46.525
Oh, on Instagram, sure.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:48.695
♪♪

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.630
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:54.300
♪♪

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.937
♪♪

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.972
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:02.441
[ Laughter continues ]

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.243
♪♪

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.311
Yeah, and it bends.

00:04:05.311 --> 00:04:07.813
Oh, yeah, oh,
he can walk with it. Yep.

00:04:07.813 --> 00:04:10.215
-Yeah, it's -- They always show
that it's portable.

00:04:10.215 --> 00:04:11.550
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.686
That's a great impression.
-I see these all the time.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.988
-I knew exactly
what you were doing.

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:19.825
I want to talk about your movie
"Mitchells vs The Machines."

00:04:19.825 --> 00:04:22.028
You know, this has been
the number-one movie on Netflix

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:23.662
for two straight weeks.

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:24.663
Ever single day,
the number-one movie.

00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:25.631
That's a pretty big hit.

00:04:25.631 --> 00:04:26.733
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:29.168
-It's very funny.
It's funny for adults.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.604
It's funny for adults and kids.
My kids love it.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.639
But also,
I was laughing out loud.

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:35.275
It's well, well done.
Congratulations.

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:37.009
-I thought they did a great job.
Thanks.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:40.146
It was -- Me and Beck Bennett
play robots.

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.148
-Yeah.
-Sort of malfunctioning robots.

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.849
So, yeah.

00:04:43.849 --> 00:04:46.119
-Is that -- Is that it?

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.154
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:51.990
Fred?

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.125
Fred, can you hear me?

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:54.894
Fred, my Zoom --
-Yeah, yes, I can hear you.

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.395
That's it, you know?

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:58.263
I don't -- I don't want to

00:04:58.263 --> 00:05:00.199
go into the whole thing
about the whole movie.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.234
It's just --
-Why?

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:03.802
Why not?

00:05:03.802 --> 00:05:05.805
-I'm worried about how much time
I'm taking up --

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:08.440
Do you want me to go into
what the movie is about?

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.043
-Just do the beginning,
at least.

00:05:11.043 --> 00:05:13.146
-Okay, so,
open on title sequence.

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:14.613
-Ah, forget it!
Forget it.

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:16.316
It's gonna take too long.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.917
Title sequence.
Here we are. Back again.

00:05:18.917 --> 00:05:21.454
Here we go.
And there we go.

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:23.356
-What is it that you want?
-I try to explain to you.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:24.824
-What is it --
-And then you --

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:27.393
-Can I speak? Can I speak?
-And I go --

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.895
And then I try --
-Can I -- No. No.

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:31.363
You asked me --

00:05:31.363 --> 00:05:33.699
-You said --
-You asked me distinctly.

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:35.968
You --
-I wish I had a mirror.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.103
-You asked me --

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:38.670
You said, "What is the movie
about?"

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:39.538
-To show you what
you looking at.

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:42.575
No, I said to you --
-No.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:44.110
What did you say?

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.878
I want everyone to hear
what you said.

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:47.780
You tell everyone.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.716
What did --
-Don't tell me what to do!

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:53.353
You tell everyone what I said.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.188
-You -- I'll tell you
what you said.

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.556
You said you didn't know.
-That's right.

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:59.759
And I meant it.
And I meant I didn't know.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.261
And I didn't know
what the movie was about.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:04.496
All right? I'm sorry.
Okay?

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:07.266
-It's a robot apocalypse.
There!

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.836
Now no one is going to see it
'cause they know what it is.

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:11.437
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:14.206
-It's already the number-one
freakin' movie on Netflix!

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:15.407
-But who's watching it?!

00:06:15.407 --> 00:06:17.309
-The whole world's watching it!

00:06:17.309 --> 00:06:20.746
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:20.746 --> 00:06:22.948
I want to show a clip
from the movie.

00:06:22.948 --> 00:06:24.850
Here's the very funny
Fred Armisen

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:26.452
in "The Mitchells vs
The Machines."

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:27.753
Take a look.

00:06:27.753 --> 00:06:29.455
-We are robots.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.457
Let us go downstairs
and find the humans

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.125
who you cannot give orders to.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:34.494
-Okay, cut it out.
-Hold on.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:36.596
I kind of want to see
where this is going.

00:06:40.867 --> 00:06:43.201
[ Can clatters, marker squeaks ]

00:06:43.201 --> 00:06:44.937
[ Footsteps approach ]

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.940
-Glad those "robots" are gone.

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:51.710
-Now it's just us humans
with our very human faces.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:53.012
-All right.
I just turned the corner.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.013
I like these guys.

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:57.883
-Yes.
My human guy name is Eric.

00:06:57.883 --> 00:07:00.552
-My name is also Eric.

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:04.557
-No. I mean Debra...
Bot 5,000.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.191
-Idiot!

00:07:06.191 --> 00:07:09.428
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Fred Armisen, everybody!

00:07:09.428 --> 00:07:12.365
"The Mitchells vs the Machines"
is available now on Netflix.

